---
slug: sign-in/email-link
method: post
layout: ''
searchable: false
metadata: {
    page_name: "Email Me a Sign-In Link - Submit",
}
---

{%- liquid
  if context.current_user
    redirect_to '/dashboard'
    break
  endif

  comment
    A post without a valid authenticity token is not refused: it arrives with an empty
    session. The form page sets this flag, so its absence means the token was missing or wrong.
  endcomment
  if context.session.sign_in_form != 'on'
    redirect_to '/sign-in/email-link?error=session'
    break
  endif

  assign email = context.params.email | default: '' | strip | downcase
  assign valid = true
  if email.size < 6 or email.size > 254 or email contains ' '
    assign valid = false
  endif
  unless email contains '@'
    assign valid = false
  endunless
  unless valid
    redirect_to '/sign-in/email-link?error=invalid'
    break
  endunless

  comment
    The link is built from the SITE_ORIGIN constant, never from the request, so nobody can
    make the email point at another site by changing a header. Without it, no link is sent.
  endcomment
  assign origin = context.constants.SITE_ORIGIN | default: '' | strip
  assign last_char = origin | slice: -1, 1
  if last_char == '/'
    assign origin_size = origin.size | minus: 1
    assign origin = origin | slice: 0, origin_size
  endif
  if origin == blank
    redirect_to '/sign-in/email-link?error=unavailable'
    break
  endif

  comment
    An instance with no sendable sender (see emails/sender) cannot send, so none is promised.
  endcomment
  function sender = 'emails/sender'
  unless sender.ok
    redirect_to '/sign-in/email-link?error=unavailable'
    break
  endunless

  comment
    5 requests per address and 20 per IP address in 15 minutes. Every request counts the
    same whether or not the address has an account, so the limit tells nobody which do.
  endcomment
  function allowed = 'account/rate_limit/allow', action: 'sign_in_link', key: email, max_per_key: 5, max_per_ip: 20
  unless allowed
    redirect_to '/sign-in/email-link?error=too_many'
    break
  endunless

  function return_to = 'account/safe_return_to', path: context.params.return_to
  function ip = 'account/rate_limit/client_ip'
  function account = 'account/sign_in/allowed_user', email: email

  assign now_unix = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  assign expires_at = now_unix | plus: 900 | date: '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'
  assign nonce = 40 | random_string
  assign status = 'miss'
  if account.id != blank
    assign status = 'pending'
  endif

  comment
    One row and the same answer for every address. Only an address with an account gets
    an email. The platform token is sent in the link and never stored; the row keeps the
    nonce, which is what makes the link work once.
  endcomment
  graphql saved = 'account/sign_in/create_link_request', email: email, nonce: nonce, expires_at: expires_at, status: status, ip: ip, return_to: return_to

  if status == 'pending' and saved.record_create.id != blank
    graphql minted = 'account/sign_in/mint_link_token', email: email, hours: 0.25
    if minted.user.temporary_token != blank
      assign encoded_email = email | url_encode
      assign encoded_token = minted.user.temporary_token | url_encode
      assign encoded_nonce = nonce | url_encode
      assign link = origin | append: '/sign-in/link?e=' | append: encoded_email | append: '&t=' | append: encoded_token | append: '&n=' | append: encoded_nonce

      assign mail = {}
      assign mail['to'] = email
      assign mail['link'] = link
      assign mail['minutes'] = 15
      graphql sent = 'account/sign_in/send_sign_in_link', data: mail
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Keep the table small: requests live 15 minutes, so anything older than a day can go.
  endcomment
  assign day_ago = now_unix | minus: 86400 | date: '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'
  graphql cleared = 'account/sign_in/delete_old_requests', table: 'sign_in_link', before: day_ago

  redirect_to '/sign-in/email-link?sent=1'
-%}
